# WHAT THE EVIDENCE DOES NOT ANSWER. The absence census over the documents that attest to a
# real system.
#
# ⭐⭐ READ THIS AS A MAP OF THE MODEL'S EDGES. Every row is a question somebody was asked and
#    declined, with the reason they gave -- so `unmeasured` rows are where an instrument would
#    buy something, `none` rows are settled findings, and `notApplicable` rows are places the
#    schema asks a question that does not arise. The three call for completely different work
#    and a NULL would have made them one column of silence.
-- reports/absence_census.sqlc at corpus scope.
:compose(reports/absence_census.sqlc, @scope = scope/corpus.sqlc)
